New opt-in option `--modular-termination` (experimental; it does not yet establish termination in every program).  With it, `decreases {:global} E` declares a method's or function's global bound.  A call dispatched to a bodyless member of a trait whose implementations may lie in other modules is rejected unless the callee's global bound is below that of the member making the call, and a call to known code that can reach such a dispatched call is rejected unless the callee's global bound is at most the caller's, so a helper that forwards a dispatched call needs a bound of its own.  Calls through function values are not checked, so a program can still prove `false` under the option.  With `--show-hints`, it reports every call that needs one of the rules.
